{
  "dom_id": "step-e8227",
  "name": "Example: Traces of Cylinders",
  "problem": "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cylinder $\\dfrac {x^2} 2 +  \\dfrac {(y-2)^2}4  = 1?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the cylinder, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ y-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =2\\pm 2 \\\\ y & =0,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of two lines $y=0$ and $y=4$ in the $yz$-plane.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
